WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:02.103
A useful way to read requirements is

00:00:02.129 --> 00:00:04.037
to look for different kinds of language

00:00:05.795 --> 00:00:10.284
Nouns often suggest candidate entities Descriptive
facts

00:00:10.310 --> 00:00:14.889
often become attributes Verbs often reveal
relationships

00:00:15.810 --> 00:00:18.179
Words such as must may only and

00:00:18.205 --> 00:00:20.916
at least often reveal constraints or optionality

00:00:22.671 --> 00:00:25.552
For example patient and provider are nouns

00:00:26.489 --> 00:00:28.555
Birth date is a descriptive fact about

00:00:28.581 --> 00:00:31.739
a patient A patient books an appointment

00:00:31.765 --> 00:00:35.515
describes a relationship Every appointment must have

00:00:35.542 --> 00:00:40.380
one provider describes a required relationship Do

00:00:40.394 --> 00:00:44.597
not start by typing CREATE TABLE Start

00:00:44.610 --> 00:00:46.518
by writing the business meaning in plain

00:00:46.531 --> 00:00:50.297
language Once the meaning is clear translating

00:00:50.323 --> 00:00:52.481
it into a relational structure becomes much

00:00:52.507 --> 00:00:53.034
easier
